  "security_implications": "The chunk aggregates multiple security-critical error signals (sparse FSM errors, count errors, storage errors) into a single err_o, which could mask the source of integrity violations. Lifecycle escalation enable is synchronized and distributed to the SHA3 and entropy engines; any glitch or inconsistency in lc_escalate_en could defeat security disablement. Message masking (msg_mask_en) is gated with a handshake, but relies on correct external configuration and valid data transfer. The unused run_req_o and tied run_ack_i may hide internal backpressure that could affect secret state. Combined error OR-ing without local clear may lead to stuck err_o, potentially blocking recovery from transient faults.",
  "evidence_refs": [
